The QA test defines `_GRAY = "0.371825413792"` and every test method passes that same string to `_colors._to_rgba_no_colorcycle(..., None)`. In `lib/matplotlib/colors.py`, `_to_rgba_no_colorcycle` handles string inputs by trying named-color and hex-color cases first; this literal matches none of those, so it reaches the “string gray” block, where `c = float(c)` makes `c` equal to `0.371825413792`. The next check is `if not (0 <= c <= 1):`, and because that float is within the inclusive interval `[0, 1]`, the subexpression `(0 <= c <= 1)` is `true`.

